{"availability":"available","full":"yadava5/applied","name":"applied","description":"Job search tracker that reads your Gmail inbox, sorts every message into the right application, and sends anything it is unsure about to a review queue instead of guessing. Next.js 16 and FastAPI on Supabase Postgres with row level security. Try the demo without an account.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-02-09T20:21:27Z","updated":"2026-10-01T07:45:38Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://getapplied.vercel.app","topics":["email-classification","fastapi","gmail-api","job-search","machine-learning","mlops","nextjs","nlp","oauth2","onnx","postgresql","python","react","row-level-security","setfit","supabase","text-classification","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://getapplied.vercel.app/demo","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T09:23:38.357Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T09:23:38.357Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T09:23:38.357Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T07:21:23.576Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T09:23:38.357Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Applied turns a job-search inbox into a pipeline. Connect your mail and every confirmation, rejection, interview invite and take-home lands on the application it belongs to — instead of in a spreadsheet that is wrong within a week.","Live app · Status & access · Try it, no account · Privacy · System Card · What you can check · Licensing","The reason to trust a product that reads your mail is not a promise; it is something you can open. Applied publishes specific numbers about itself and scripts/readmefacts.py recomputes every registered one of them from the code that defines it — an unregistered number, or a registered one whose site nobody pointed at the file holding it, is unchecked — readme-facts.yml fails the build when a claim on this page stops matching the source, and a claim reworded so the checker can no longer find it fails too. Where each number terminates is in Verify it."],"features":["The classifier is deterministic, and it is not an LLM. Classification is regexes, an","The body is read to classify, then discarded. Applied fetches the full message because","Nothing is filed for you below the confidence gate. A prediction under the gate goes to a","A metric that names its stage. The rules layer — 220 regex patterns, no model — scores 0.9896 macro-F1 on the 96-example v3 evaluation set, committed at backend/data/evaluation/baselinerulesv3.json. backend-ci.yml fails…","Cost measured per layer, not averaged. SetFit costs roughly 100× the rules layer at p50 — 17.649 ms against 0.176 ms — and the rules layer answers 174 of the 288 classifications in the benchmark run. That is the cascade…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yadava5/applied/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"34a28d7434f3aeb622b274c24dd63d147eb034e96b896955a3dd270d20d21258","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T07:21:23.785Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T07:21:23.785Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Applied turns a job-search inbox into a pipeline. Connect your mail and every confirmation, rejection, interview invite and take-home lands on the application it belongs to — instead of in a spreadsheet that is wrong within a week.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yadava5/applied/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"Live app · Status & access · Try it, no account · Privacy · System Card · What you can check · Licensing","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yadava5/applied/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Fixture demo — the full UI on synthetic data at /demo, no login.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yadava5/applied/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"34a28d7434f3aeb622b274c24dd63d147eb034e96b896955a3dd270d20d21258","sourceUrl":"https://github